  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "The sum of an infinite geometric series of positive terms is 9. If the first two terms are removed, then the sum of the resulting geometric series is 1. Find the first two terms.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a_1=6$ and $a_2=2$.\n\nThe remaining sum is $r^2$ times the original sum, so $r=\\frac13$.",
      "worked": "Let the first term be $a$ and the common ratio be $r$. Positive terms and convergence require $0<r<1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{a}{1-r}&=9\\\\\\frac{ar^2}{1-r}&=1\\\\r^2&=\\frac19\\\\r&=\\frac13\\end{align*}$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=9(1-r)\\\\a&=9\\left(1-\\frac13\\right)\\\\a&=6\\\\a_2&=6\\left(\\frac13\\right)\\\\a_2&=2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
  },
